[21.020242000000003,"o","● The app is loading again: I restarted the backend and all three services\r\n  now report healthy.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCause:\u001b[0m the database was restarted at 11:14:40 (\u001b[94minfra restart -s db\u001b[0m, run\r\n  from the CLI by a person). That cut the backend's Postgres connection\r\n  with \u001b[94mterminating connection due to administrator command\u001b[0m. The backend\r\n  crashed on an unhandled pg error. Its watch-mode dev script stayed alive\r\n  waiting for a file change, so the service showed \u001b[94mrunning, not ready\u001b[0m. The\r\n  frontend went not-ready because it depends on the backend.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m \u001b[94mstackctl --mode development service restart -s backend\u001b[0m. Backend,\r\n  frontend and worker are now \u001b[94mrunning, ready\u001b[0m, and the db and mail infra\r\n  are up.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mUnderlying bug:\u001b[0m the backend has no error handler on its pg pool, so any\r\n  future database restart will crash it the same way. Adding a\r\n  \u001b[94mpool.on('error', …)\u001b[0m handler, or reconnect logic, in the backend would\r\n  fix that. I haven't changed any"]
[21.020335542,"o"," code. Want me to look at it?\r\n\r\n"]
